From 127d63b337eb7a6aff985a73d57a58f981f21b5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:20:33 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 090/130] render: a shape's placeholder picture is 1 x 1
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A shape has no picture (its passes compile with DIRECTDRAW and read none), but the placeholder
an image without a texture gets was made at the layer's size: a square of the scene's height,
18 MB at 3840 x 2160 (3319542538: 548 → 530 MiB, as before shapes drew).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md "F2 result" (cost)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
index 4ca6768..41e1230 100644
--- a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
+++ b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
@@ -110,8 +110,10 @@ CImage::CImage (Wallpapers::CScene& scene, const Image& image) :
 	// https://docs.wallpaperengine.io/en/scene/scenescript/reference/event/cursor.html same applies to effects
 	// TODO: create a dummy texture of correct size, fbo constructors should be enough, but this should be properly
 	// handled
+	// (a shape's picture is never sampled: DIRECTDRAW. 1 x 1, not its square of the scene's height)
+	const glm::vec2 dummy = isShape ? glm::vec2 (1.0f) : size;
 	this->m_texture = std::make_shared<CFBO> (
-	    "", TextureFormat_ARGB8888, TextureFlags_NoFlags, 1, size.x, size.y, size.x, size.y
+	    "", TextureFormat_ARGB8888, TextureFlags_NoFlags, 1, dummy.x, dummy.y, dummy.x, dummy.y
 	);
     }
 
